  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the cooperative corporations law and the not-for-profit\ncorporation law, in relation to requiring the board of directors of\nresidential cooperative corporations and not-for-profit corporations to\nprovide tenants with changes to the by-laws in writing within ten days of\nadoption; in relation to notification to tenants of changes affecting\noccupancy or the rules of the building",
    "basePrintNo": "S4956",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4956-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §16, add §78, Coop Corps L; amd §602, add §624, N-PC L",
    "lawSection": "Cooperative Corporations Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4956\n\nSPONSOR: BENJAMIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the cooperative corporations law and\nthe not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to requiring the board\nof directors of residential cooperative corporations and not-for-profit\ncorporations to provide tenants with changes to the by-laws in writing\nwithin ten days of adoption; in relation to notification to tenants of\nchanges affecting occupancy or the rules of the building\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill ensures that residents are provided with timely written\nnotification of changes to governing by-laws by their buildings' boards\nof directors.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 16 of the cooperative corporations law.\n\nSection two amends section 602 of the not-for-profit corporation law by\nadding a new paragraph (g).\n\nSection three sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIndividuals who own a condominium or shares in a cooperative are subject\nto rules and by-laws created by a board of directors. While this direct\nrulemaking is a democratic process, there is no legal requirement that\nthe board of directors notify shareholders of new rules or changes to\nexisting rules.\n\nThis bill requires boards of directors to provide residents with written\nnotice of any changes to the building's governing by-laws within 10 days\nof the changes to ensure that each owner's interests are protected.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017-18: A.3830 - Ordered to Third Reading Calendar\n2015-16: A.6870 - Referred to Housing\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill shall take effect on the sixtieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "printNo": "S4956",
