    "lawCode": "Amd §708, BC L; amd §602, add §624, N-PC L",
    "lawSection": "Business Corporation Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4956A\n\nSPONSOR: BENJAMIN\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill ensures that residents are provided with timely written\nnotification of changes to governing by-laws by their buildings' boards\nof directors.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends § 708 of the business corporation law to require cooperatives to\nnotify members of changes in their by-laws.\n\nAmends § 602 and § 624 of the not-for-profit corporation law to require\ncooperatives to notify members of changes in their by-laws.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nn/a\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIndividuals who own a condominium or shares in a cooperative are subject\nto rules and by-laws created by a board of directors. While this direct\nrulemaking is a democratic process, there is no legal requirement that\nthe board of directors notify shareholders of new rules or changes to\nexisting rules.\n\nThis bill requires boards of directors to provide residents with written\nnotice of any changes to the building's governing by-laws within 10 days\nof the changes to ensure that each owner's interests are protected.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017-18: A.3830 - Ordered to Third Reading Calendar\n2015-16: A.6870 - Referred to Housing\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill shall take effect on the sixtieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
